name c02m01-insurrection
timeout 300
time 1998-10-13T17:00:00Z

# DELTA FORCE (NovaLogic 1998), CAMPAIGN ONE "PERU", FILE SLOT C02M01, PLAY ORDER 1 OF 6 --
# {Insurrection}, working title "C02M01 - Clear Camp", Objective BREEZE, designer Steve McNally [BMS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/delta-force/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [CAMP]: "Eliminate the mercenary detachment located at Objective Breeze."
# Goal M01SUBGOAL01: "Eliminate all enemy soldiers at Objective Breeze." No extraction goal, and the
# mission carries no extraction aircraft [BMS] -- the two facts agree, 3 of 3 / 0 of 3 across the
# campaign.
# THE RADIO [DLG], the whole of it: "Proceed southwest and neutralize all hostiles."
# THE FIELD [BMS]: 492 objects, footprint 1052 x 771 m, insertion point (-187.6,-108.0), enemy
# centroid (-380.2,-301.4) = 273 m at 225 deg -- and 225 deg is what "southwest" says, one of the six
# checks that fix +x = east / +y = north. Terrain C2M1.TRN "Jungle Terrain 1", day, high sun.
# THE CAST: 58 hostiles -> `target_soft` on the D5 lattice (pitch 118.3 m) - 4 Squad Member (5002) ->
# friendly `target_soft` at their measured range/bearing from the IP: Alpha 129 m/146 deg and
# 131 m/142 deg, Charlie 232 m and 236 m/287 deg [BMS], the pair whose 1 m and 5-8 m agreement with the
# briefing's "approximately 130 meters" and "about 240 metres" is what proves the METRE - one
# `tower, guard` (3014) at (-370.6,-373.2), neutral.
# NOT DECLARED, for want of a coordinate rather than a mechanism (D5): the two building groups of 3
# and 4 parts, and the 2 vehicles (type 2009). The research recorded their COUNT and nothing else.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `bravo2`'s.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires `kill team hostile` -- all 58 -- and nothing else: campaign.md 10 says the
#   hostile-alive count reaching zero IS the verdict, so a run that clears the camp and then dies
#   walking home still passed, and that is why this file declares no `survive`.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading. Report the COUNT of dead hostiles; that number is the measurement
#   this file exists to take, and D8 bounds it at one aim point.
#   exit 2 = an airframe departed controlled flight with nobody having shot it: an ENGINE finding,
#   since nothing in this mission can shoot at all (D2).

# ---- THE NINE DISCLOSURES THAT APPLY TO ALL SIX FILES. Stated in full HERE; the other five carry
# ---- the short form and point back at this file.
#
# D1  THERE IS NO MAN ON FOOT IN THIS TREE AND NONE WAS INVENTED (CLAUDE.md Prinzip 1). Bravo Two, one
#     soldier walking, flies as `module f16`. This is the largest substitution in any of the five mods
#     and its error is total, not directional:
#       SPEED    the original walks. 300 kt = 154.3 m/s against a walking 1.4 m/s = 110x. 300 kt is the
#                lowest run-in speed measured to survive `set task attack`'s egress (mods/comanche D1);
#                nothing slower is available, because below it the jet mushes in.
#       HEIGHT   the original's eye sits at 1.7 m standing [MAN p.14, the three-posture icon]. Every
#                file flies its pass at 150 m = 88x, and there is no lower number: see D7.
#       POSTURE  stand / crouch / prone are three contact sets with three eye heights. Nothing in
#                doc/body-format.md is implemented; there is one posture and it is `airborne`.
#       LOS      every mission in this campaign is decided by whether a position 200-500 m away
#                OVERLOOKS the objective (terrain.md 1). There is no terrain LOS query at man height,
#                and D6 removes the terrain as well.
#       COVER    hostiles stand behind barrels, in windows and in a guard tower. Without occlusion
#                those placements carry no meaning, and the guard tower here is a soft block.
#
# D2  THE HOSTILE SOLDIER IS A TENT, AND HE DOES NOT SHOOT BACK. Types 5005/5006/5007/5041 ->
#     `target_soft`, the softer of the tree's TWO ground classes; `target_hard` is the other one, and
#     no third exists, so this is a substitution with no refused alternative. Two errors, both large:
#     the class carries a +-10 m damage zone and a 2.8e3 structural fail threshold for a man 0.5 m
#     wide who dies to one rifle round; and a ground unit has no weapon against another ground unit.
#     MEASURED in this round: a hostile `zsu23` at 200 m from a friendly `target_soft`, 120 s, ZERO
#     weapon events, both INTACT. The firefight -- which is the whole of all six missions -- is deleted.
#     `target_hard` is used NOWHERE in this campaign: no object in the six missions is armoured.
#
# D3  THE PRIMARY WEAPON HAS NO TARGET. The M4, the MP5, the SAW, the M40A1 and the Barrett all fire
#     bullets, and `modules/ground/FBGroundTarget.h` states in its own source why that cannot reach a
#     ground object: presented area and extent are ZERO "because gun bundles are resolved against
#     aircraft only". Every file declares `set gun_rounds 30` -- one M4 magazine [MAN p.8] -- and it
#     fires nothing at anything, in every run. What CAN be delivered is the secondary: 2 satchel
#     charges [MAN p.9] -> 2 x `mk82`, 227 kg against roughly 10 kg. The 6 fragmentation grenades, the
#     M203, the laser designator, the Ka-Bar and the claymores have no row and no mechanism.
#
# D4  THE NAVIGATION QUANTUM IS LARGER THAN THE MISSION. `systems/FBNavSystem`'s waypoint capture
#     radius is 500 m, a default argument, and it is NOT in `--pilot-keys`: a mission cannot change it.
#     Four of the six missions' entire briefed ingress fits inside ONE capture radius -- Insurrection
#     273 m, Weatherman 308 m, Masquerade 367 m, Headhunter 406 m -- and in Weatherman and Masquerade
#     the objective and the extraction point are 450.0 m and 506.7 m apart, so the second goal of each
#     is met by not moving. MEASURED separately on a `target_soft` given a flight plan: a waypoint
#     391 m away is WP_REACHED `by=capture` at t = 0.1 s from a unit that never moves and cannot.
#
# D5  THE SOLDIER LATTICE, AND WHY IT CANNOT FLATTER THE RESULT. The research recorded each mission's
#     hostile COUNT, its measured CENTROID and its measured FOOTPRINT, not the per-record coordinates
#     (campaign.md 6). The N records are therefore laid on a square lattice centred on the measured
#     centroid with pitch sqrt(EW*NS/N) -- count, centroid and areal density measured, arrangement
#     reconstructed, and one record sits exactly ON the centroid so that the aim point is not decided
#     by the parity of a grid. MEASURED in this round, over the five deliveries: everything within
#     31.3 m of an impact died and nothing beyond 61.2 m did. The lattice pitch is 118-235 m, i.e.
#     twice the widest kill measured, so NO bomb ever gets two lattice neighbours -- unlike
#     mods/comanche, where the source data's own stacking raised the yield, nothing here is stacked.
#     A group with a MEASURED EXTENT (Flood's airfield, Weatherman's Objective Gale, Headhunter's
#     villa) is laid on that extent instead; a group with a
#     centre but no extent is ONE object carrying its part count in a comment; a group with neither is
#     NOT DECLARED, and each file lists what it therefore omits.
#
# D6  THE GROUND IS FLAT AND IT IS NOT PERU'S. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, so every altitude here is
#     ASL and AGL at once. And this is a CHOICE against available data, not an absence: `fb-tiles`
#     DOES cover the Alto Huallaga -- MEASURED in this round at the six box centres of terrain.md 5,
#     629.30 / 537.00 / 516.55 / 638.00 / 281.90 / 688.72 m, which closes terrain.md's own "fb-tiles
#     coverage for Peru is unverified" gap and confirms its 274-1458 m band from below -- but
#     `mod.json` names no "dem", because a baked raster is untracked by rule (doc/assets.md) and a
#     mission is a test that must run without a server. What is lost is exactly
#     what terrain.md 1 says every mission needs: 74-267 m of relief and a position that overlooks
#     another.
#
# D7  THE RUN-IN IS LONGER THAN THE CAMPAIGN. `set task attack` anchors its run-in leg at the phase's
#     first tick and never corrects a lateral offset (measured for mods/comanche: 249-8382 m across
#     track when spawned on the game's own heading). Every striker here therefore spawns ON the bearing
#     from the game's insertion point to its aim point, 3 000 m out -- 4x to 11x the mission's own
#     insertion-to-objective distance, and outside all six of terrain.md 5's bounding boxes. The
#     game's insertion point is not the spawn; it is the last point on the run-in before the target.
#
# D8  ONE STRIKER IS ONE AIM POINT. Measured for mods/comanche and unchanged here: `set task attack`
#     releases at the ACTIVE waypoint, flies its egress and hands back to `Route`, and nothing in the
#     format or in FBPilot re-enters it. Delta Force sends ONE man, so there is not even a wingman to
#     make it two -- one aim point against 33 to 96 hostiles, and that ratio is this campaign's headline.
#
# D9  THE CLOCK. Date 1998-10-13 -- the single dated artefact in the whole source set, the Manual
#     Addendum's own date stamp [MAN], because the game data carries no date at all. The instant per
#     mission is chosen to reproduce terrain.md 8's measured `.TRN` preset (day / night / dusk) at
#     Peru's UTC-5, and it is CHECKED, not asserted: the runner's `mission CLOCK` line prints the
#     computed sun elevation at the striker's spawn, and the six measure +87.48 / +62.13 / +57.85 deg
#     for the three the .TRN calls day, -69.11 / -73.05 deg for the two it calls night, and -1.10 deg
#     for Headhunter, which the .TRN calls sunset and which is civil twilight to a tenth of a degree.
#
# WHAT COULD NOT BE DECLARED AT ALL, each a missing engine capability rather than a missing asset:
#   the three postures (D1) - ground line of sight and therefore cover (D1) - a CARRIED MISSION ITEM
#   (`Carrying: Code Book` [GAME]: the unit model has no slot, so Masquerade's first goal degrades to
#   an overflight) - a MOVING CONVOY (Bad Habit's 1 891 m route is three AI chains of 12 nodes; there
#   is no ground mover in this tree, movers are aircraft, so the nine vehicles stand still) - foliage
#   (Bad Habit's 73 + 120 palms are not units) - the six briefings, the 34 radio lines and the 11 goal
#   texts AS TEXT (a .fbm carries a reading rule for a machine) - spawn delays and difficulty-scaled
#   enemy counts (a .fbm is not a schedule) - and CAPTURE: "he must be taken alive" is expressible only
#   as `protect unit druglord`, which is not the same statement.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`, `--threads 1/2/4` byte-identical): ONE OF FIFTY-EIGHT.
#   t = 11.6 s   ATTACK_RELEASE ccrp accepted at 150.0 m and 171.5 m/s ground speed, throw 918.4 m,
#                the CCRP solution's own predicted miss 23.3 m
#   t = 12.2 s   ONE Mk-82 away, station 3 -- and station 7 is still loaded at t = 300: `set task
#                attack` is one pass and one release, so the game's TWO satchel charges are one here
#   t = 14.7 s   wp0 `by=capture`. The run-in took 14.7 s; a man walking this mission's 1052 m edge at
#                1.4 m/s needs 751 s, and the striker crosses it in 6.1 s
#   t = 18.0 s   impact 31.3 m from the aim point. `h001` -- the one hostile record standing ON the
#                measured centroid -- is destroyed. The `tower, guard` at 50.1 m survives the same burst
#   guns         ZERO events in 300 s with 30 rounds loaded, against 58 men (D3)
#   verdict      TIMEOUT, `kill team hostile` 1 of 58. The 57 that live were never engaged by anything:
#                there is one aim point (D8) and no second weapon that reaches the ground (D3).

unit bravo2
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn -8.96924 -76.13985 150 242.9 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  set gun_rounds 30
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set cmds_mode off
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp -8.98152 -76.16414 150 300
  wp -8.99380 -76.18842 1000 300
  objective kill team hostile

unit h001
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn -8.98152 -76.16414 ground 18.0 0

